This is a list of avaliable LLMs on my hosted Proxmox instance and the allowed settings.
There are "red", "Yellow" and "Green" models, this refers to hosting cost (ie VRAM usage)
"Red" LLMs use all/most of the 24GB of VRAM avaliable so please limit useage where possible but will normally provide the best answers
"Yellow" LLMs will use about half so two users can use them simultaneously
"Green" LLMs are low VRAM usage so the cost/impact on others is minimal
"Black" LLMs that are listed but wont run, dont try them, they are expensive to run
Lists are in rough order of quality

Settings - 
Flash attentnion can improve performance, can be unstable, try it?
Context window depends on the model, 4k is default, 8k is enough for most things, models are worse at larger context windows so try to keep your chats short

Name Format - 
Using "R Qwen 3 30B A3B Q4 XL (unsloth)" as example
"R" if it is a reasoning model (thinks before responding)
"Qwen" Name
"3" Version
"30B" Parameters (more usually higher quality, slower, more expensive)
"A3B" active parameters if relevant
"Q4" precision
"XL" quant quality
"(unsloth)" labeled model provider (provider of disstillation)

